595 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This explains how Confucian principles, particularly Li, serve as a means for social control. When individuals consistently practice propriety and moral education, they also internalize their roles within society, reinforcing the hierarchical structures that sustain the filial piety principle. In this sense, control is not imposed coercively but rather cultivated through strict adherence to the tradition which Confucius sets up himself.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
