625 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Filial piety imposes strict expectations of obedience and sacrifice, often making individuals silence their emotional struggles out of fear of disrupting the family reputation. Likewise, social harmony, when interpreted as the avoidance of conflict and the prioritization of external appearances, reinforces the idea that psychological distress should be handled privately, if not concealed entirely. Families, therefore, chose internal problem-solving over professional consultation, not because of a lack of need, but because Confucian ideals make external intervention feel culturally inappropriate.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
