794 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The British East India Company's \(BEIC\) taxation policies not only hindered industrial growth but also oppressed individual economic freedom, forcing enticeable workers into exploitative labor conditions. As India's industrial strain intensified, over 68% of the workforce suffered from labor displacement and got transferred into the unpredictable agricultural sector during the post-rule of the BEIC in 1900. Amidst the BEIC's heavy tax duties on Indian products, combined with cheap British imports, traditional industry modernization of exquisites like textiles and handicrafts significantly declined. The East India Company's colonial rule not only hindered industrial growth but also expanded its oppressive policies to other sectors, particularly unique artisanal businesses. )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
