/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (After the independence of India on August 15th, 1947, the British-Indian military was formally divided into the Pakistan Armed Forces and the Indian Armed Forces. In the years following partition, the Indian military primarily played the role of a constabulary force, as shown through both the integration of the princely states and through the role that the Indian Military played in maintaining order due to the disorganisation of the Indian civil government, especially in once disputed territories such as Junagadh and Kashmir.  )
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [4]
>>
