1009 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (I. INTRODUCTION )
/Pg 53 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1010 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In the age of artificial intelligence and space exploration, ancient Greek mythology might seem like a relic of the past. Yet, these timeless tales continue to captivate our imagination and offer profound insights into timeless human nature and societal structures. A recurring motif within these myths is the intervention of gods and goddesses in the lives of mortals. This literature paper examines existing scholarship research on divine intervention in Greek mythology, focusing specifically on how such interventions differ for male and female mortals and what these differences reveal about Greek cultural attitudes towards women during the Classical period. Furthermore, how this goes on to suggest the normalised manhandling of women stemmed from the norms and attitudes showcased in the myths passed down in society. )
/Pg 53 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
