1031 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Greek myths frequently depict goddesses exercising formidable influence, delivering severe punishments to mortals as a way to assert their dominance and highlight cultural fears surrounding female authority. In the multiple myths of Hera and Alcemna, Io, Semele, Hercules, Athena and Arachne, Aphrodite and Psyche, Helen, Atalanta, Demeter and Persephone, Medusa and Athena, Artemis and Callisto. These tales were widespread with fear and caution underlining the power of female gods, and the malice that runs through them if you dare defy their order. The disagreeable punishments given to female mortals in most cases go to extreme lengths that would be considered unnecessary, showcasing anxiety around female power. )
/Pg 54 0 R
/K [6]
>>
