/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Throughout the myths of divine intervention consisting of interaction between female mortals and female gods, the main themes are ones of unfair punishments and the frequent urge to control female power. Though the women may undergo sexual assault or were wronged in a competitive environment and the men are to blame, the women are almost always blamed. These myths normalised this behaviour in classical society as men told women that these served as cautionary tales against higher power, and they took relief that the myths simply reinforced societal norms. )
/Pg 56 0 R
/K [5]
>>
