/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (As we move on to the extent of expectations that female gods held towards mortal men, I will be examining the circumstances in the myths between them which typically involve guidance, assistance and the reinforcement of heroic ideals. While the gods bestowed gifts upon mortals, they expected male heroes to wield the gifts with power and glory most often to complete quests and achieve greatness or win over a woman, whereas when female mortals were given gifts it was often under guise of punishment for perceived misused of divine favor or for exceeding prescribed boundaries.While these stories portray women as supportive figures who contribute to male success and maintaining social order, they are thereby reinforcing traditional gender roles where women's primary role is to empower men. The male mortals simply receive aid from the respectful female gods, who do not confuse aid with ill intentions. The patterns here offered by the female gods are incredibly more mundane and heartfelt compared to the ones by male gods to female mortlas. The myths I will go through will divulge the simplicity of the female gods actions and how this corresponds with how female mortals had to act in society, and in regards to mortal ment. In doing so, we can solidify our understanding about the expectations in attitudes that women were forced to uphold. )
/Pg 58 0 R
/K [6]
>>
