/T (The ways in which female gods interacted with male mortals were often pure-hearted and primarily involved guiding and gifting. In scenarios where they got involved with male mortals, regarding leniency and love in some cases, it was with consent from both parties. In cases with gifts and guidance, myths such as Athena and Odysseus, Hera and Jason, Athena and Perseus, Athena and Heracles, Athena and Achillies, and Hera and Paris are ones that come to mind the easiest. These stories all portray female gods as the bringer of gifts and wisdom. When emotions are heightened between female gods and male mortals, stories such as Aphrodite and Adonis, Artemis and Hippolytus, Aphrodite and Paris, and Artemis and Orion are notable myths. Due to the opposing nature of the expectations and attitudes of female gods and male gods when it comes down to interacting with mortals, we will be analysing the circumstances between female gods and male mortals, and how these stories portray women as supportive figures who contribute to male success and maintaining social order, they are thereby reinforcing traditional gender roles where women's primary role is to empower men. )
