/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The fact that the husband to the goddess of marriage is the reason for over fifty percent of infidelities warrants our immediate attention, showcasing that there is not only a power play among gods and mortals, but within the gods themselves. It is known that the goddesses, no matter how powerful, must ask Zeus for permission before commencing their deeds. Athena, the goddess of warfare, must ask Zeus before intervening in war. These myths act as a mirror, even though the women have been so incredibly wronged, they are discarded for and left on the side. This is portrayed in society when they held little to no regard for women's well being in ancient Greece. )
/Pg 60 0 R
/K [4]
>>
