/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Regarding the myths between male gods and male mortals, the primary type of stories where they interact are where the god is offering a gift or imparting wisdom on the mortal. The second more uncommon type is where there are romantic relationships, though it is mostly with Apollo or Dionysus. The stories of Zeus and Hector, Apollo and Orpheus, Hermes and Odysseus, Poseidon and Theseus, Zeus and Perseus and Zeus and Achilles all showcase the gods passion in carrying out their legacy and helping mortal men, with little to no stipulations. The romantic myths with Apollo and Hycinthius. And then simply the paternal myths with Apollo and Asclepius, and an opposite one of Apollo and Phaethon. These tales showcased the glorification of the trials that the men go through, whereas the female mortals often received little to no recognition. )
/E (Regarding the myths between male gods and male mortals, the primary type of stories where they interact are where the god is offering a gift or imparting wisdom on the mortal. The second more uncommon type is where there are romantic relationships, though it is mostly with Apollo or Dionysus. The stories of Zeus and Hector, Apollo and Orpheus, Hermes and Odysseus, Poseidon and Theseus, Zeus and Perseus and Zeus and Achilles all showcase the gods passion in carrying out their legacy and helping mortal men, with little to no stipulations. The romantic myths with Apollo and Hycinthius. And then simply the paternal myths with Apollo and Asclepius, and an opposite one of Apollo and Phaethon. These tales showcased the glorification of the trials that the men go through, whereas the female mortals often received little to no recognition. )
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [3]
