/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (While some may argue these myths reflect broader themes of divine order or cautionary lessons, the consistent blaming and suffering of women cannot be overlooked. These stories reveal how ancient Greek society justified unequal treatment of women and reinforced restrictive gender norms. So to answer the question, what extended to the differences in divine intervention for men and women in Greek mythology reveal Greek cultural attitudes towards women during the classical period? The patterns across both bodies, female and male, mortal and god, showcase that the attitudes and expectations regarding women were significantly lower and more derogatory in myths, which served as guidelines in regular society during the classical period. )
/Pg 62 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1123 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Understanding the significance of these myths is important because they shaped foundational cultural values for the world. By examining ancient narratives, we see how far society has progressed in gender equality and inclusivity as a whole, and why it remains crucial to challenge lingering stereotypes rooted in these early stories. These stories show us where we have been- and inspire where we must go. )
/Pg 62 0 R
/K [5]
>>
