/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The purpose of this paper is to discover whether there are societal, economic and cultural differences in Zoroastrian society in Iran versus India. The argument this paper constructs is two fold, firstly that the Zoroastrian society pre-conquest was susceptible to a divide because of the over-integration of the religion and the location of the followers and secondly that due to this a divide has manifested in the categories listed above. The key findings of the paper can be found in Section 2 where the differences are extrapolated from current information on the two societies.)
/Pg 66 0 R
/K [4]
>>
