/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Analysis of data on the social, economic, and cultural standing that Zoroastrians have had in Iran and India after the Arab conquest of Persia in 651 CE, denotes a significant divide built between the Parsis in India and the Iranian Zoroastrians. This immediate divergence is representative of the consequently and conversely much larger and long-term differences between the two societies and the impact that has had on the religion. )
/Pg 67 0 R
/K [4]
>>
