1253 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This continuous discrimination meant that the Iranian Zoroastrians had to pick up rural jobs, such as farming, to avoid discrimination in big cities. Often, these rural farmers also live in Zoroastrian enclaves such as Yazd or Kerman. This discrimination has had vast economic impacts as it has locked them into a cycle of poverty that will likely continue for generations to come as agriculture is not a particularly prosperous industry in Iran with lots of competition over not so much land.)
/Pg 75 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
